title: Rogue DHCP Server / DHCP Spoofing
id: 168ebe12-860c-4461-ab27-0557ec7988ea
status: experimental
description: Detects DHCP OFFER/ACK packets from an unauthorized server, a rogue-DHCP technique used to assign a malicious gateway or DNS server for man-in-the-middle interception.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1557/003/
logsource:
  category: network_connection
detection:
  selection:
    protocol: 'dhcp'
    dhcp_message_type:
      - 'OFFER'
      - 'ACK'
    server_authorized: false
  condition: selection
fields:
  - src_ip
  - src_mac
falsepositives:
  - Newly added but legitimate DHCP servers
level: high
tags:
  - attack.credential_access
  - attack.t1557.003
